## Issues

### Active (none)

No active issues found in the 2026-04-26 QA pass.

### Closed (QA pass 2026-04-26 — prior cycle active items, both verified resolved)

- [x] `src/service/install/provisionBrain/obsidianBrainAideTemplate/index.ts` lines 53–58 (Prose body string literal)
  **VERIFIED RESOLVED.** The `## Prose` body section does NOT contain a CLAUDE.md navigation pointer. Current content (lines 53–58) correctly reads: "The vault has two entry hubs: the coding-playbook hub at `coding-playbook/coding-playbook.md` and the research hub at `research/research.md`." Both hubs ARE scaffolded by the pipeline. The prior todo.aide's [x] was accurate — the fix landed before this QA pass ran.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` — "Scaffolding a vault-root CLAUDE.md as part of the brain contract... is rejected." The Prose body now points only to artifacts that exist on a cold install.
  Misalignment: (none — resolved)

- [x] `src/service/install/provisionBrain/index.test.ts` — missing test for MCP step drift-on-brain-key branch
  **VERIFIED RESOLVED.** Test `5g` (lines 693–737) covers the "brain key present but entry differs" branch. The test pre-writes a valid brain.aide, pre-writes a .mcp.json whose brain entry deliberately differs, runs provisionBrain, and asserts: `mcpStep.status === "would-overwrite"`, `mcpStep.prescription.key === "brain"`, and that the prescription matches the derived entry from brain.aide rather than the stale on-disk entry. All 77 tests pass (confirmed via `rtk vitest run`). The prior todo.aide's [x] was accurate.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` — the fourth implicit migration branch (brain key present, entry differs) is now covered.
  Misalignment: (none — resolved)

